                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4152681185",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cl has a −1 charge, so the charge on Pt is +2 (+2 + 4(−1) = −2). This complex is an anion, so the suffix "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "-ate"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is added to the stem of the name of the metal. The metal ion is Pt"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", which is named as platinate(II)."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1899552062",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This complex is named tetrachloroplatinate(II) ion."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "603729059",
                "type": "p"
